-- title:
--   Residue-field point above a crossing point of the mod-p fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a package $\mathfrak{X}$ of data `DRModelPackage p` on the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` over $\mathbb{Z}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` with respect to `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, with structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$ and whose residue field is algebraically closed, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. The package supplies two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ from the $\kappa$-rational model $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$ to the base change of `DRModel p` along $\mathbb{Z}\to\kappa$. The assertion is that for every point $x$ of the fibre product of these two morphisms there exists a morphism $s$ from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field of $O$ to the base change of `DRModel p` along $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,O$ such that $s$ followed by the second projection is the identity, i.e. $s$ is a section over the residue field, and such that the image of $x$ in the base change along $\mathbb{Z}\to O$, obtained by applying the first projection, then $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$, then `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, equals the image under `DRModel.baseChangeMap (IsLocalRing.residue O)` of the value of $s$ at the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field.
--
--   The statement says that each crossing point of the two components of the Deligne–Rapoport fibre at $\kappa$ is, after specialisation into the model over $O$, the image of a point with values in the (algebraically closed) residue field of $O$. It serves as the rationality input for reading the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model at the residue field, and is used in the construction of node coordinates, in the production of sections over the base from vanishing Abel–Jacobi classes, and in the identification of widths in the resolved package.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_exists_residueField_point_baseChangeMap_eq_of_isAlgClosed_residueField.lean

